      "title": "Enforce output bounds before files enter Iris capture directory",
      "path": "/private/tmp/native-jax-callback-tpu-bootstrap.py",
      "line_start": 63,
      "line_end": 73,
      "detail": "The worker writes directly below IRIS_OUTPUT_DIR. After exit, bootstrap checks count/types/bytes and raises on an overrun, but leaves those files present. Iris captures application-error outputs as well. Scientific write() writes each <=2MiB file before checking its16MiB total, then its finally block can write report.json. Thus an overrun can exceed the declared17MiB archive payload despite bootstrap rejecting it.",
      "requested_change": "Stage gate output outside IRIS_OUTPUT_DIR, validate complete allowed regular files and byte/count bounds, then copy only a valid complete gate into capture directory; retain small failure metadata on invalid output. Repack and refreeze command and recapture SDK request.",
      "root_response": "Accepted; root plans isolated TemporaryDirectory stage,<=30 scientific files/2MiB each/16MiB total before copy. Targeted response recheck required; fix not yet reviewed."
    }
